id: index_error
category: exceptions
difficulty: 4
libs:
checker: exact
timeout: 10
--- prompt
Write an Objeck program that creates an Int array of size 3, then reads element 5 inside a try block (use a variable for the index) and catches the out-of-range access with an `on` clause for IndexError, printing `out of range`. After the try statement print `after`. Output: `out of range` then `after`.
--- expected
out of range
after
--- reference
class IndexCheck {
	function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
		values := Int->New[3];
		index := 5;
		try {
			values[index]->PrintLine();
		}
		on(e : IndexError) {
			"out of range"->PrintLine();
		};
		"after"->PrintLine();
	}
}
